    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Names and politeness",
     "texto": [
      "**老师** means «teacher»; like «teacher» in English, it has no masculine or feminine form. **学生** means «student».",
      "**你好** is a greeting, and **谢谢** means «thank you». **再见** is used to say goodbye. Write proper names with Chinese characters when you know them; here there are also foreign names transcribed into Chinese."
     ],
